y.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident architect of the Toll War who suppresses Wren's access to the bridges. When her charts show a Cartel trade route will fall with the failing bridge, he is forced to weigh his monopoly against his own fleet. He ends by suspending tolls for repair crews, though only after being pressed by the combined Wardens and Hollow Circle.","personality_traits":["calculating","courteous","ambitious","controlling"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Control","description":"He directs Cartel shipping lanes and can close routes to those who defy him.","category":"social"},{"name":"Contract Leverage","description":"He binds others through contracts and wind-debts that are hard to escape.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_maribel_thatch","name":"Maribel Thatch","role":"supporting","description":"A weathered, sturdy miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted grey braids and a booming laugh. She leads the Hollow Circle's resistance to the Cartel's grain levy.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"She wants to keep the archipelago fed and her people free from Cartel levies.","goal":"Defeat the Grain Levy and secure safe grain shipments across the bridges.","flaw":"She distrusts outsiders and scholars and refuses help that comes from anyone but her own.","internal_conflict":"She believes in the self-reliance learned in the Great Calm, but knows the Hollow cannot survive without the failing bridges.","external_conflict":"The Cartel levy threatens her mills while the unstable bridges delay grain shipments.","arc":"Maribel starts out refusing to deal with Academy outsiders. When a damaged bridge strands a grain shipment and Wren's charts show a safe crossing window, she cautiously accepts help. She ends by pledging Hollow Circle labour to repay the crew's wind-debt and standing beside the Wardens against the levy.","personality_traits":["blunt","generous","stubborn","warm"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Mastery","de