{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A former Bridge Warden inspector turned private investigator, Mara is in her late forties, with rain-darkened coats, a limp from a skybridge snap years ago, and grey streaks she no longer dyes. She works out of a cramped office above the Mistral Docks fish stalls, taking cases the Wardens and Cartel will not touch.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that truth can still be bought without being sold, after her own mentor's name was ruined by a lie.","goal":"Unmask the blackmailer and break the web of false alibis before the next victim is ruined.","flaw":"She trusts documents and timelines over people, and dismisses anyone whose story she cannot verify.","internal_conflict":"She fears she left the Wardens because she was complicit in a cover-up, and that her current crusade is penance rather than justice.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants the blackmailer's ledger kept buried, and the Wardens will not open their crossing logs to her.","arc":"Mara begins as a cynical loner who believes only paper evidence. When she finds that Tobias Reen's airtight alibi was forged to protect his daughter, she must choose between exposing a sympathetic liar and bending her rule. She chooses to weigh motive alongside proof, ending as an investigator who accepts human testimony and finally reconciles with her Warden past.","personality_traits":["dry-witted","stubborn","observant","weary","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crossing-log analysis","description":"Reads wind-debt ledgers and skybridge crossing records to detect false alibis.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bridge-sense","description":"Judges a skybridge's structural condition by sound and sway, useful for tailing suspects across the isles.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_silas_quill","name":"Silas Quill","role":"antagonist","description":"A soft-spoken cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained cuffs and a courteous smile. Silas has spent decades charting skybridge routes and quietly noting who crosses where and when, which has given him a private archive of other people's secrets.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To escape the crushing wind-debt he owes by turning other people's secrets into income.","goal":"Collect enough payments to clear his debt and buy passage out of the archipelago before the Academy audits his charts.","flaw":"He is vain about his cleverness and cannot resist leaving taunting, tidy clues for those he considers beneath him.","internal_conflict":"He tells himself he only exposes hypocrites, yet he hates that he has become the thing he despises.","external_conflict":"Mara is closing in on his pattern of leaked crossing records, and one of his victims has threatened to expose him first.","arc":"Silas starts as a self-justifying, patient extortionist who sees himself as a neutral observer. When Mara traces a forged alibi back to his charts, he escalates by blackmailing Tobias Reen's daughter. The act shatters his illusion of detachment, and he ends by surrendering his archive to Mara in a bid to limit the damage, accepting his guilt.","personality_traits":["polite","calculating","vain","patient","resentful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route forgery","description":"Alters skybridge crossing charts to fabricate or erase alibis.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Quiet leverage","description":"Reads people's hidden fears and frames demands so victims comply without protest.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_reen","name":"Tobias Reen","role":"supporting","description":"A heavyset Drift Cartel shipping clerk at Mistral Docks in his fifties, with salt-cracked hands and a ledger always under his arm. He is a doting father known on the docks for his punctuality and the precision of his records.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep his daughter Wren from being dragged into Cartel debts and scandal.","goal":"Keep the forged alibi covering Wren's night of illicit crossings from unravelling.","flaw":"He lies instinctively and believes any deception is justified for family.","internal_conflict":"He is an honest clerk by trade and is tormented by falsifying the very records he swore to keep true.","external_conflict":"The blackmailer's demands and Mara's questions both threaten to expose Wren's unpaid wind-debt crossings.","arc":"Tobias starts as a man defending his daughter with lies. Pressured when Silas threatens Wren, he must decide whether to keep paying or tell Mara the truth. He confesses his forged alibi and testifies against the blackmailer, ending as a father who protects Wren through honesty instead of deceit.","personality_traits":["nervous","loyal","meticulous","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger craft","description":"Keeps and subtly rewrites shipping records so they pass inspection.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_marrow","name":"Odalys Marrow","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-tongued Drift Cartel enforcer in her thirties with a braided silver-threaded queue and a leather coat slick with rain. She rises through the Cartel by solving other people's problems quietly, and she is wary of Mara.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To protect the Cartel's grain levy revenue, which funds her family's rise out of the lower docks.","goal":"Recover the blackmailer's ledger before it exposes Cartel levy practices.","flaw":"She treats loyalty as ownership and cannot tolerate being second-guessed.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the Cartel's tolls are crushing people like those she came from, yet she enforces them anyway.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy conflict is turning the Hollow Circle against the Cartel, and her superiors expect her to silence Mara's inquiry.","arc":"Odalys starts as a loyal Cartel fixer who intends to bury Mara's investigation. When she learns the ledger contains evidence the levy was inflated by her own superiors, she chooses to hand Mara a key crossing record. She ends estranged from the Cartel but free of its leash.","personality_traits":["blunt","ambitious","guarded","efficient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dockside intimidation","description":"Uses reputation and menace to extract information from dock workers.","category":"social"},{"name":"Close combat","description":"Fights without open flame or gunpowder, using weighted cord and knives.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_reen","name":"Wren Reen","role":"supporting","description":"Tobias's twenty-two-year-old daughter, a part-time courier and apprentice miller with flour-dusted sleeves and quick, watchful eyes. She moves between Mistral Docks and The Hollow carrying small parcels for hire.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To earn enough to pay off her mounting wind-debt and free her father of worry.","goal":"Hide the unregistered night crossings that she used to carry grain to starving farmers during the levy.","flaw":"She is impulsive and takes risks without telling anyone.","internal_conflict":"She resents her father's smothering protection but depends on his lies to stay safe.","external_conflict":"Silas's blackmail and the Cartel's grain levy put her at risk of seizure by Cartel agents.","arc":"Wren starts as a reckless courier hiding her crossings from everyone. When Silas's demand reaches her, she goes to Mara herself instead of letting her father lie. She ends owning her actions openly and negotiating her wind-debt repayment through labour in The Hollow.","personality_traits":["bold","resourceful","impulsive","compassionate"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windrider","description":"Navigates skybridges at night using wind currents to avoid checkpoints.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_silas_pursuit","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_silas_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Voss hunts Silas Quill, the blackmailer, after tracing leaked crossing records to Silverspine; he in turn tries to mislead her with taunting clues."},{"id":"rel_silas_tobias_extortion","source_character_id":"chr_silas_quill","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_reen","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Silas Quill extorts Tobias Reen by threatening to reveal the forged alibi that covers Wren's illicit crossings."},{"id":"rel_mara_tobias_interrogation","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_reen","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Voss presses Tobias Reen on his airtight alibi, and he stonewalls her to protect his daughter."},{"id":"rel_odalys_mara_wary","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Odalys Marrow shadows and warns off Mara Voss for the Cartel, yet gradually becomes an uneasy ally when the ledger implicates her superiors."},{"id":"rel_tobias_wren_family","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_reen","target_character_id":"chr_wren_reen","relationship_type":"family","description":"Tobias Reen shields his daughter Wren with lies, while Wren resents the protection that keeps her silent."},{"id":"rel_wren_mara_trust","source_character_id":"chr_wren_reen","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Reen comes to Mara Voss with the truth about her night crossings, giving Mara the break she needs against Silas Quill."}]}
