{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","description":"A forty-year-old salvage captain from Mistral Docks, weathered and wiry, with salt-grey braids and a scarred left hand from a cable accident. She has spent two decades hauling wreckage from the drifting lanes to pay off a ruinous wind-debt her late husband left behind. She wears a patched oilskin coat and carries a brass sounding-line that was his.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To clear the wind-debt that has bound her family to the Cartel for fifteen years.","goal":"Bring home enough salvage from the liner to buy her crew out of Cartel service.","flaw":"Stubborn pride that makes her refuse warnings and help from others.","internal_conflict":"She fears that abandoning the liner's riches means her husband's death was for nothing.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel will seize her crew's skyship if the debt is not repaid within the season, while the fog-bound liner traps them.","arc":"Mara begins as a captain who will risk anyone to settle her debt. When the liner's fog seals the exits and she must choose between a vault of Cartel-valued cargo and rescuing Joss from the lower decks, she drops the cargo. She ends the story humbled, accepting the debt's consequences and trusting her crew's counsel over her pride.","personality_traits":["stubborn","resourceful","guarded","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Navigation","description":"Reads wind and drift by sounding-line and sound alone when sight fails.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Crew Command","description":"Holds a frightened crew together with blunt, steady orders.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_pell","name":"Joss Pell","description":"A twenty-three-year-old rigger and cable-braider from Emberroost, lean and freckled, with soot-darkened fingers. He signed onto the crew to escape the forge-island's rigid guild life. He talks constantly when nervous and keeps a notebook of bridge-knot patterns.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove he is more than a junior braider and earn a Warden master's mark.","goal":"Document the liner's unusual cloudstone rigging so the Wardens will recognise his skill.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity that overrides his caution.","internal_conflict":"He wants Warden approval yet resents the guild that treated him as disposable.","external_conflict":"The liner's rigging is shifting by itself and the vanished passengers seem to lure him deeper into the lower decks.","arc":"Joss starts as an eager rigger who wanders off alone to sketch the rigging. Lured below by a voice mimicking Mara, he is trapped and nearly lost, then saved by the crew. He ends the story cautious, putting survival before recognition and cutting loose his need for the guild's approval.","personality_traits":["curious","talkative","eager","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Reads and repairs cloudstone cable with expert hands.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_elias_crane","name":"Elias Crane","description":"A gaunt sixty-year-old former liner steward, long presumed lost, who now haunts the ship as its caretaker. His pale, fog-dulled eyes and immaculate uniform hide the fact that he has been feeding the ship's hunger for decades to keep it afloat. He greets the crew with practiced hospitality.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the liner and its remaining passengers from ever being scattered or forgotten.","goal":"Bind the salvage crew to the ship as new passengers so the fog never lifts.","flaw":"Possessive devotion that cannot tolerate anyone leaving.","internal_conflict":"He remembers being a living man and secretly longs to be released, yet fears ending the only purpose he has left.","external_conflict":"Mara's crew intends to strip and tow the liner, which would break the fog that sustains him.","arc":"Elias begins as a courteous host concealing the ship's hunger. When Mara refuses his offer to trade a crew member for the rest's safe passage, he is forced to confront his own captivity. He ends by letting the fog thin and the liner drift apart, accepting release.","personality_traits":["courteous","patient","melancholy","manipulative"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Binding","description":"Draws the ship's fog around intruders to seal exits and muffle their voices.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Echo Mimicry","description":"Reproduces voices of the living to lure them deeper into the ship.","category":"supernatural"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_joss_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_joss_pell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Voss acts as a gruff mentor to Joss Pell, whose recklessness repeatedly forces her to choose between protecting him and pursuing salvage."},{"id":"rel_elias_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_elias_crane","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Elias Crane sees Mara Voss as a thief of the ship and tries to bind her crew to the liner, opposing her plan to strip it."},{"id":"rel_elias_joss_lure","source_character_id":"chr_elias_crane","target_character_id":"chr_joss_pell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Elias Crane targets Joss Pell as the easiest crew member to lure, using mimicked voices to pull him away from Mara Voss."}]}
