tly when nervous and keeps a notebook of bridge-knot patterns.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove he is more than a junior braider and earn a Warden master's mark.","goal":"Document the liner's unusual cloudstone rigging so the Wardens will recognise his skill.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity that overrides his caution.","internal_conflict":"He wants Warden approval yet resents the guild that treated him as disposable.","external_conflict":"The liner's rigging is shifting by itself and the vanished passengers seem to lure him deeper into the lower decks.","arc":"Joss starts as an eager rigger who wanders off alone to sketch the rigging. Lured below by a voice mimicking Mara, he is trapped and nearly lost, then saved by the crew. He ends the story cautious, putting survival before recognition and cutting loose his need for the guild's approval.","personality_traits":["curious","talkative","eager","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Reads and repairs cloudstone cable with expert hands.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_elias_crane","name":"Elias Crane","description":"A gaunt sixty-year-old former liner steward, long presumed lost, who now haunts the ship as its caretaker. His pale, fog-dulled eyes and immaculate uniform hide the fact that he has been feeding the ship's hunger for decades to keep it afloat. He greets the crew with practiced hospitality.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the liner and its remaining passengers from ever being scattered or forgotten.","goal":"Bind the salvage crew to the ship as new passengers so the fog never lifts.","flaw":"Possessive devotion that cannot tolerate anyone leaving.","internal_conflict":"He remembers being a living man and secretly longs to be released, yet fears ending the only purpose he has left.","external_conflict":"Mara's 