eed without her.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens, locked in the Toll War with the Cartel, are racing to reach the city first.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident financier who treats the expedition as a transaction. When the jungle consumes his hired guards after he forces a march against Mara's warning, he is left stranded and humbled. He ends either consumed by the city he sought to plunder or reduced to bargaining for survival.","personality_traits":["polished","ruthless","patient","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt contracts to bind and coerce others into service.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ironhand_dessa","name":"Dessa Ironhand","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, Dessa has forearms scarred by cable-braiding and a booming laugh. She joins the expedition to inspect ancient cloudstone found in the ruins.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To discover the lost builders' cloudstone technique to strengthen the skybridges.","goal":"Recover samples of the original cloudstone and bring them safely to the Wardens.","flaw":"She is rigidly loyal to Warden orders and ignores evidence that contradicts them.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between duty to the Wardens and her growing respect for Mara's judgment.","external_conflict":"The Toll War makes Cartel members like Corvin her natural enemy while she must share the expedition with them.","arc":"Dessa starts as a by-the-book Warden suspicious of everyone. When Corvin's Cartel guards threaten to cut the expedition's only rope-bridge over a ravine, she defies Warden orders to cooperate with Mara. She ends as a pragmatic ally who values people over protocol.","personality_traits":["loud","loyal","practical","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Constructs and repairs rope and cloudstone-cable crossings.","category":"technological"},{"n