who is controlled by it.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tiberon_crass","name":"Tiberon Crass","description":"A charismatic man in his forties with a booming voice and an easy, open smile, who rose from a dockside rope-hauler to the people's champion. He dresses plainly to appear one of the crowd, though his rings are bought with Cartel gold.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To seize lasting power so no one can again make him powerless or poor.","goal":"Win emergency control of skybridge tolls and wind-debt collection by whipping the crowds into demanding it.","flaw":"Cannot tolerate dissent and escalates to cruelty when his image is threatened.","internal_conflict":"He half believes his own promises to the poor, yet knows the Cartel's patronage makes them lies.","external_conflict":"Marcellus Vane's scheming and the Bridge Wardens' refusal to cede bridge control threaten to unmask him.","arc":"Starts as a confident populist who believes he can serve the people and the Cartel at once. When Marcellus exposes Cartel payments during the Senate session and the crowd turns on him, he orders the Mistral Docks gates shut against the Wardens, revealing his tyranny. He ends as an exposed demagogue who has lost the genuine affection he secretly craved.","personality_traits":["charming","vindictive","insecure","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crowd Command","description":"Sways large gatherings with rhetoric and showmanship.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_lysandra_quill","name":"Lysandra Quill","description":"A broad-shouldered miller in her late thirties with flour-dusted braids and sun-lined eyes, elected speaker of the Hollow Circle after the Great Calm stories of her grandmother shaped her belief in self-reliance.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's farmers from the Cartel's grain levy and the hunger it would cause.","goal":"Secure a Senate ruling that voids the Cartel's grain levy.","flaw":"Distrusts every outsider, which makes her reject useful help.","internal_conflict":"She wants the Hollow to remain quietly self-sufficient but knows isolation will not stop the levy.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy on grain shipments strains her people, and Crass's agents threaten to blacklist Hollow barges.","arc":"Starts as a guarded speaker who refuses to leave the Hollow's politics. After Marcellus admits his past error to her face, she weighs the risk and chooses to travel to the Senate and testify against the levy. She ends as a public voice for the Hollow, trusting selective allies without surrendering her independence.","personality_traits":["stubborn","practical","protective","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Signal Network","description":"Coordinates farmers across the isle through windmill vane signals.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_halcyon","name":"Oren Halcyon","description":"A soot-streaked Bridge Warden engineer in his forties with burn-scarred forearms, who braids cloudstone cables at Emberroost and lives by the no-flame rule.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe from tolls that starve their maintenance.","goal":"Prove to the Senate that Cartel tolls are being diverted away from bridge repair.","flaw":"Obsessive perfectionism that makes him conceal doubts and refuse to delegate.","internal_conflict":"He feels guilty that a cable he braided once failed, and fears being blamed again.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves the Wardens underfunded while Crass's mobs blame them for crossings turned dangerous.","arc":"Begins as a lone, secretive engineer hiding a past cable failure. When Crass's followers threaten the Emberroost forge-pits, Oren admits the failure publicly and trains junior Wardens to share the work. He ends as a leader who shares responsibility and gives Marcellus the repair ledgers.","personality_traits":["meticulous","secretive","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Skilled at braiding and inspecting cloudstone skybridge cable.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_vane_crass_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tiberon_crass","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marcellus Vane schemes to expose Tiberon Crass, whose rise as a demagogue is built on the same toll crisis Marcellus once failed to resolve."},{"id":"rel_crass_vane_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tiberon_crass","target_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tiberon Crass mocks Marcellus Vane to the crowds as a fallen elitist, amplifying public scorn against him."},{"id":"rel_vane_quill_ally","source_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","target_character_id":"chr_lysandra_quill","relationship_type":"reluctant ally","description":"Marcellus Vane needs Lysandra Quill's testimony against the grain levy, but she distrusts his motives and demands his honesty."},{"id":"rel_halcyon_vane_ally","source_character_id":"chr_oren_halcyon","target_character_id":"chr_marcellus_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Oren Halcyon supplies Marcellus Vane with repair ledgers, but his secrecy about his past cable failure strains their trust."},{"id":"rel_crass_quill_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tiberon_crass","target_character_id":"chr_lysandra_quill","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tiberon Crass uses the Cartel's grain levy to pressure Lysandra Quill and threatens to blacklist the Hollow's barges."}]}
