{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kest_vael","name":"Kest Vael","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered wanderer in her late thirties, born on The Hollow to a family of millers. She is lean and sun-darkened, with a wrapped scarf of grey linen and eyes narrowed from years of squinting into bright, hard light. She left home after the Grain Levy emptied her family's stores and now carries only a waterskin, a cloudstone-thread rope, and a battered survey compass. Her speech is spare and she trusts the ground more than people.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To reach the far shore of the glass desert and learn whether the grain her family lost was ever sold there, so the debt on her name can be settled.","goal":"Cross the desert of glass alive and bring back proof of where the levied grain went.","flaw":"Stubborn self-reliance: she refuses help and hoards water and information alike.","internal_conflict":"She wants to belong to the Hollow Circle again but believes needing anyone makes her the burden that ruined her family.","external_conflict":"The wind-debt she accrued crossing skybridges comes due this season, and the Drift Cartel has sent a collector after her.","arc":"Starts as a solitary traveller who rations everything, including trust. At the midpoint, dying of thirst in the glass, she must accept Orrin Tash's offered water, a choice forced by the pursuing wind-debt and the failing of her pride. She ends the journey willing to share her proof and her route with the Hollow Circle, no longer refusing help.","personality_traits":["taciturn","observant","stubborn","dry-humoured","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Glass-reading","description":"She can judge which sheets of glass will hold weight by their colour and ring when tapped.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Thread-splicing","description":"She braids and repairs cloudstone rope in the field, a skill learned from Emberroost cable-makers