{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kest_vael","name":"Kest Vael","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered wanderer in her late thirties, born on The Hollow to a family of millers. She is lean and sun-darkened, with a wrapped scarf of grey linen and eyes narrowed from years of squinting into bright, hard light. She left home after the Grain Levy emptied her family's stores and now carries only a waterskin, a cloudstone-thread rope, and a battered survey compass. Her speech is spare and she trusts the ground more than people.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To reach the far shore of the glass desert and learn whether the grain her family lost was ever sold there, so the debt on her name can be settled.","goal":"Cross the desert of glass alive and bring back proof of where the levied grain went.","flaw":"Stubborn self-reliance: she refuses help and hoards water and information alike.","internal_conflict":"She wants to belong to the Hollow Circle again but believes needing anyone makes her the burden that ruined her family.","external_conflict":"The wind-debt she accrued crossing skybridges comes due this season, and the Drift Cartel has sent a collector after her.","arc":"Starts as a solitary traveller who rations everything, including trust. At the midpoint, dying of thirst in the glass, she must accept Orrin Tash's offered water, a choice forced by the pursuing wind-debt and the failing of her pride. She ends the journey willing to share her proof and her route with the Hollow Circle, no longer refusing help.","personality_traits":["taciturn","observant","stubborn","dry-humoured","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Glass-reading","description":"She can judge which sheets of glass will hold weight by their colour and ring when tapped.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Thread-splicing","description":"She braids and repairs cloudstone rope in the field, a skill learned from Emberroost cable-makers.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_tash","name":"Orrin Tash","role":"antagonist","description":"A lean, polished debt collector in his fifties employed by the Drift Cartel at Mistral Docks. He wears a salt-stained coat with brass buttons and carries a ledger bound in basalt-grey leather. Once a dockhand who rose by memorising every debt in the harbour, he regards unpaid wind-debt as a moral failing rather than a misfortune.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a permanent seat among the Cartel's merchant princes by never letting a single debt go uncollected.","goal":"Catch Kest Vael before the season ends and collect her wind-debt in full.","flaw":"Rigid literalism: he cannot see anything outside the ledger as worth weighing.","internal_conflict":"He privately suspects the Grain Levy was unjust but has built his identity on believing the ledger is always right.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's rising tolls and the Toll War strain his superiors' patience, and a failed collection could cost him his post.","arc":"Starts as a certain, merciless collector. In the glass desert, when Kest's evidence shows the levied grain was misreported, he must choose between the ledger and what he sees, a conflict rooted in the Grain Levy. He ends by sharing his water with her and striking her debt from his book, breaking his rigid literalism.","personality_traits":["meticulous","cold","patient","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger memory","description":"He recalls every debt, date and sum he has ever recorded.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cartel authority","description":"His seal compels dock officials and skippers to aid his pursuit.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_maren_sol","name":"Maren Sol","role":"supporting","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy, small and ink-stained, with white hair cropped short and spectacles repaired with copper wire. She once taught Kest to read charts and still sends her letters tucked into cloudstone-thread spools.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To complete a final chart of the glass desert before her eyesight fails entirely.","goal":"Get Kest's field notes back to Silverspine so the chart can be finished.","flaw":"Detachment: she values maps over the people who risk their lives to make them.","internal_conflict":"She is proud of her student yet guilty that her request sent Kest into danger.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens press the Academy to prioritise skybridge surveys over the desert chart, threatening her funding.","arc":"Starts as a cloistered scholar who treats explorers as data sources. When news arrives that Kest is lost in the glass, she defies the Wardens' funding order and travels toward Mistral Docks to arrange a search. She ends having chosen a person over a chart.","personality_traits":["precise","warm in private","absent-minded","determined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge cartography","description":"She can chart drifting bridge routes from sparse observations.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_orrin_pursues_kest","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_tash","target_character_id":"chr_kest_vael","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orrin Tash hunts Kest Vael as the Drift Cartel's collector, determined to claim her unpaid wind-debt, which drives her flight across the glass desert."},{"id":"rel_kest_mentee_maren","source_character_id":"chr_kest_vael","target_character_id":"chr_maren_sol","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Kest Vael was taught chart-reading by Maren Sol and carries her request to map the desert, a bond that pulls Kest toward the Academy and away from solitude."},{"id":"rel_maren_vs_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_maren_sol","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_tash","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Sol opposes Orrin Tash's attempts to seize Kest's field notes as collateral, setting Academy scholarship against Cartel debt-collection."}]}
