yed silks and carries a brass tally-ring. Born to a Cartel family, she signed her first shipping contract at sixteen and knows every wind-debt owed in the archipelago.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep her family's trade lanes alive and secure the Cartel's standing in the face of the common enemy.","goal":"Broker the three-city alliance on terms that keep Cartel shipping lanes open and profitable.","flaw":"Calculating to a fault; she prices every relationship and expects the same of others.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her success rests on debts she has exploited from people she secretly respects.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy: the Hollow Circle refuses her levy, threatening the alliance she needs to broker.","arc":"Veyra starts as a transactional negotiator who leverages wind-debts. When the Hollow Circle's elder Maro Thistledown forgives a debt rather than collect it during the Grain Levy standoff, she waives the levy herself. She ends valuing trust above leverage.","personality_traits":["shrewd","charming","guarded","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Memory","description":"Recalls every debt, price and contract she has seen.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuasive in tense negotiations.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_maro_thistledown","name":"Maro Thistledown","description":"An elderly miller and elder of the Hollow Circle, Maro has white hair tied in a flour-dusted braid and hands knotted from decades at the windmill gears. He survived the Great Calm as a boy and remembers the hunger of that decade. He speaks softly and rarely leaves The Hollow.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To ensure no child in the archipelago ever starves as he did during the Great Calm.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's grain levy while keeping grain flowing to every isle.","flaw":"Insular and slow to trust outsiders, he withholds help until asked three times.","internal_conflict":"He wonders if his quiet neutrality has allowed others to suffer.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy imposed by the Drift Cartel threatens to bankrupt his millers.","arc":"Maro begins as a withdrawn elder refusing to join any alliance. Facing Veyra's levy at the docks, he chooses to forgive her family's wind-debt and offer grain freely. He ends as an active voice in the alliance council.","personality_traits":["patient","wary","kind","stoic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Understands wind patterns and grain milling better than anyone alive.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_quill","name":"Isolde Quill","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Isolde is lanky, ink-stained and perpetually squinting. Raised an orphan in the academy dormitories, she charts the shifting skybridge network and has noticed patterns suggesting the common enemy's approach route.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove her scholarship matters by mapping the threat before it strikes.","goal":"Deliver her enemy-route chart to the alliance leaders before the enemy arrives.","flaw":"Overconfident in her maps; she dismisses field reports that contradict her data.","internal_conflict":"She craves recognition but fears her work is merely academic and useless.","external_conflict":"Kael and Veyra dismiss her findings as the alliance bickers over wind-debt and tolls.","arc":"Isolde begins as an arrogant scholar who trusts only her charts. When Kael's field report shows a span shifted against her prediction, she revises her model with his data. She ends as a collaborator whose corrected map guides the alliance.","personality_traits":["brilliant","impatient","curious","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drifting bridge networks with uncanny accuracy.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_dorran_vask","name":"Dorran Vask","description":"A gaunt Cartel enforcer in his fifties with a hawk nose and a silver-capped tooth, Dorran collects overdue wind-debts for the Drift Cartel. He is a veteran of the Cartel charter's early enforcement years and views the alliance as a threat to his profession.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To preserve the old Cartel order that gave him status and security.","goal":"Sabotage the alliance by provoking the Hollow Circle and Wardens into open breach.","flaw":"Vindictive; he cannot let a slight go unanswered.","internal_conflict":"He senses the old order is dying and fears he has nothing else to be.","external_conflict":"Veyra's diplomacy threatens his enforcement role and the Toll War that sustains it.","arc":"Dorran begins as a loyal enforcer undermining the alliance. After he cuts a skybridge line near Emberroost and Kael pulls him from the falling span, he confesses his scheme to Veyra. He ends stripped of rank but alive and no longer an enemy.","personality_traits":["cold","cunning","resentful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Collection","description":"Tracks and pressures debtors across the isles.","category":"social"},{"name":"Cable Cutting","description":"Knows how to sever a bridge line with minimal trace.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kael_veyra_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_kael_ironbraid","target_character_id":"chr_veyra_dunmark","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Kael Ironbraid distrusts Veyra Dunmark because her Cartel's tolls strain the Wardens, creating friction that threatens the alliance until they learn to cooperate."},{"id":"rel_veyra_maro_opposed","source_character_id":"chr_veyra_dunmark","target_character_id":"chr_maro_thistledown","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Veyra Dunmark pushes the grain levy on Maro Thistledown, who resists on behalf of the Hollow Circle, amplifying conflict over the alliance terms."},{"id":"rel_isolde_kael_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_quill","target_character_id":"chr_kael_ironbraid","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Quill supplies Kael Ironbraid with maps of the skybridges, while Kael's field knowledge challenges her certainty."},{"id":"rel_dorran_kael_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_dorran_vask","target_character_id":"chr_kael_ironbraid","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Dorran Vask plots to sever Kael Ironbraid's bridges and discredit the Wardens, provoking the clash that tests the alliance."},{"id":"rel_dorran_veyra_subordinate","source_character_id":"chr_dorran_vask","target_character_id":"chr_veyra_dunmark","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dorran Vask resents his superior Veyra Dunmark's diplomacy and secretly undermines her to preserve the Cartel's old enforcement order."}]}
