{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","description":"A forty-year-old Bridge Warden engineer at Emberroost, Maren has spent two decades braiding cloudstone cable in the forge-pits. Her forearms are scarred by cable burns, her grey-streaked hair is cropped short for safety, and she wears a soot-stained leather apron stitched with the Wardens' knot sigil. She lost her brother when a severed skybridge dropped a transit span, and the memory still shapes how she works.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To make sure no one else dies the way her brother did when a skybridge span failed.","goal":"Uncover who sabotaged the central skybridge junction and rebuild it before the season's wind-debt comes due.","flaw":"She trusts only her own calculations and refuses to delegate or share work.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between her grief-fuelled need for vengeance and the duty to unite the isles that the Wardens swore to serve.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls strangle the Wardens' repair budget while the saboteur remains at large.","arc":"Maren begins as a lone, vengeful engineer who hoards every task. When the sabotage is traced to a spark smuggled past the no-open-flame rule at Mistral Docks, she must accept help from her Cartel rival Tobias Kerrin to repair the junction in time. She ends as a leader who shares the work and credits others.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","grieving","fiercely loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing load-bearing cloudstone cable.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Stress Reading","description":"Can sense a failing span by the pitch of its hum.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_kerrin","name":"Tobias Kerrin","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel harbourmaster at Mistral Docks in his mid-fifties, Tobias wears a salt-stiffened coat with brass buttons and a ring for every lane he controls. His broad frame has softened with age, but his eyes still track every crate on the docks. He rose from a deckhand by learning exactly who owed whom wind-debt.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the Cartel's monopoly on shipping lanes secure so that his family never returns to dock poverty.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and force the Hollow Circle to accept the grain levy.","flaw":"He treats every person as a ledger entry and cannot imagine loyalty without payment.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears the Cartel's greed is hollowing out the trade it depends on, yet admitting so would betray his rise.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle both resist his tolls and levy, threatening the Cartel Charter.","arc":"Tobias starts as a hard-line toll enforcer. When the transit sabotage strands his own cargo ships and Maren Voss shows him the cost of ruined bridges, he chooses to open the Cartel's lanes to emergency relief. He ends as a reluctant ally who trades profit for stability.","personality_traits":["calculating","charming","ruthless","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Brokering","description":"Reads and leverages wind-debts to bend others to his will.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Mapping","description":"Memorises shipping lanes and wind currents across the archipelago.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_tamsin","name":"Ilse Tamsin","description":"A young cartographer of Silverspine Academy, Ilse is twenty-three, slight and ink-stained, with a braid wrapped in measuring cord. She carries rolled charts under both arms and wears spectacles patched with wire. Her talent for predicting skybridge drift won her a scholarship but left her isolated.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that cartography can predict and prevent disasters, justifying her place at the Academy.","goal":"Chart the pattern of sabotage across the skybridge network to locate the next target.","flaw":"She buries herself in data and freezes when decisions must be made under pressure.","internal_conflict":"She wants recognition for her discovery but fears being blamed if her predictions prove wrong.","external_conflict":"Academy elders dismiss her sabotage charts as speculation, and the Cartel buys access to her maps.","arc":"Ilse starts as a timid analyst who hides her charts. After her map predicts a second attack on the Hollow's bridge, she chooses to present it to Maren and the Wardens despite the elders' scorn. She ends as a confident advisor who acts on her findings.","personality_traits":["brilliant","anxious","observant","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Prediction","description":"Forecasts skybridge movement from wind and drift data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_hallow","name":"Oren Hallow","description":"A weathered Hollow Circle miller in his sixties, Oren has flour-dusted hands and a stooped back from decades at the windmills of The Hollow. His beard is white, his voice slow, and neighbours seek his counsel on everything from harvests to disputes. He remembers the Great Calm from childhood.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his community's independence, which the Great Calm taught the isle to value above all.","goal":"Resist the Cartel's grain levy without starving the isles that rely on Hollow grain.","flaw":"He is distrustful of outsiders and clings to old grudges against the Cartel.","internal_conflict":"He must choose between his stubborn self-reliance and the cooperation his people need to survive the crisis.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy and blocked skybridge shipments threaten his harvest and his neighbours' livelihoods.","arc":"Oren begins refusing any dealings with outsiders. When the sabotage cuts off the Hollow's grain shipments, he chooses to send his millers to help Maren's Wardens rebuild the bridge in exchange for safe passage. He ends as a bridge between the Hollow Circle and the other isles.","personality_traits":["wise","stubborn","patient","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Harvest Lore","description":"Knows weather and grain cycles from lifelong experience.","category":"other"},{"name":"Community Standing","description":"His word can rally the Hollow's farmers and millers.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_kerrin","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss blames Tobias Kerrin's rising tolls for starving the Wardens' repair budget, and Tobias sees her as an obstacle to Cartel profit, fuelling the Toll War between them."},{"id":"rel_ilse_maren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_tamsin","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ilse Tamsin looks up to Maren Voss as a mentor in practical engineering, while her sabotage charts challenge Maren's habit of working alone."},{"id":"rel_oren_tobias_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_oren_hallow","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_kerrin","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Oren Hallow despises Tobias Kerrin for enforcing the Cartel's grain levy on the Hollow Circle, deepening the Grain Levy conflict."},{"id":"rel_oren_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_oren_hallow","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Oren Hallow and Maren Voss become uneasy allies when the sabotage threatens both the Hollow's grain routes and the Wardens' bridges."}]}
