l"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_halde","name":"Corvin Halde","role":"antagonist","description":"A smooth, silver-haired merchant prince of the Drift Cartel, in his fifties, who dresses in dove-grey silks and keeps a ledger chained to his wrist. He built his fortune on skybridge tolls and champions the strict prohibition of arcane practice. He knows the wards are failing and has quietly profited from selling safe passage on the remaining sound spans.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the Cartel's monopoly on inter-isle trade intact as the old order decays.","goal":"Suppress news of the failing wards and raise tolls on the last safe bridges.","flaw":"Greed disguised as prudence; he cannot value anything he cannot price.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears he is profiting from a catastrophe he helped to hide.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle's resistance to the Grain Levy and Maren's investigation both threaten his ledger.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident profiteer who treats the failing wards as a market opportunity. When the Hollow Circle's grain boycott strands his ships at Mistral Docks, he is forced to choose between doubling the tolls and opening the Cartel's reserves. He ends either ruined or reluctantly generous, having finally paid a cost he could not pass on to others.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","patient","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market Manipulation","description":"Moves prices and shipping lanes through favours and debts.","category":"social"},{"name":"Wind-Debt Leverage","description":"Uses the wind-debt rule to bind rivals to labour contracts.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tessaly_brandt","name":"Tessaly Brandt","role":"supporting","description":"A freckled twenty-year-old miller's daughter from the Hollow, with flour-dusted braids and a loud laugh. She leads the younger members of the Hollow Circle and keeps a hidden log of the grain shortages caused by the 