bt before the season ends so they keep the mill.","goal":"Earn enough dreamstone-claim shares to pay the debt without joining the Cartel.","flaw":"Easily led; he trusts whoever offers him a quick solution.","internal_conflict":"The dreams show him the quiet mill life he fears he is losing, making him want to stay asleep rather than fight for it.","external_conflict":"Quell holds his debt and pressures him to recruit other miners into longer dream shifts.","arc":"Starts as an obedient miner who recruits sleepers for Quell to keep his debt open. When Maren drags him from a dream during the anchor crack and he sees a fellow miner nearly fall, he refuses Quell's order and leads the Hollow workers to evacuate the sleepers. He ends as a confident voice for the miners.","personality_traits":["gentle","loyal","anxious","hopeful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain-Hardened Strength","description":"Hauls heavy loads for long hours without rest.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_sefa_lorne","name":"Sefa Lorne","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed cartographer in her twenties from Silverspine Academy, ink-stained and always carrying brass dividers. She was sent to chart how the moon's dream-field warps the skybridge network, and keeps secret notes proving the field is growing.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To earn a chair at the Academy by producing the first accurate map of the dream-field.","goal":"Chart the dream-field's boundaries and publish the findings before the Cartel suppresses them.","flaw":"Intellectual arrogance; she dismisses practical warnings from non-scholars.","internal_conflict":"She wants recognition for her discovery but suspects publication will spread the dreamstone's danger.","external_conflict":"Quell offers funding in exchange for her silence, while Maren demands her data for the removal case.","arc":"Starts as an ambitious scholar who hoards her data for personal fame. After her own map predicts a shared dream-collapse that she ignores until it strikes, she hands her complete charts to Maren at the cost of her claim to first publication. She ends as a collaborator who values safety over credit.","personality_traits":["brilliant","competitive","observant","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Field Cartography","description":"Maps invisible phenomena by cross-referencing instrument drift and dreamer reports.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_idris_opposition","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_idris_quell","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maren Voss, a Bridge Warden inspector, tries to halt Idris Quell's extraction, while Quell, the Cartel factor, bribes and obstructs her to keep mining."},{"id":"rel_idris_tobias_debt","source_character_id":"chr_idris_quell","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_hale","relationship_type":"creditor","description":"Idris Quell holds Tobias Hale's wind-debt and uses it to force Tobias to recruit miners into longer dream shifts, deepening the conflict with Maren."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_rescue","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_hale","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss pulls Tobias Hale from a dangerous shared dream, creating a fragile trust that eventually turns him against Quell."},{"id":"rel_sefa_maren_data","source_character_id":"chr_sefa_lorne","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sefa Lorne withholds her dream-field charts from Maren Voss, who needs them for the removal case, until the collapse forces them to cooperate."},{"id":"rel_idris_sefa_bribe","source_character_id":"chr_idris_quell","target_character_id":"chr_sefa_lorne","relationship_type":"patron","description":"Idris Quell offers Sefa Lorne funding to keep her findings quiet, tempting her to trade the colony's safety for her career."}]}
