d miller who wants to burn the Cartel's grain contracts. After Isolde warns that open flame could sever a skybridge, she chooses a disciplined grain boycott instead. She ends as a measured leader the Hollow Circle trusts.","personality_traits":["fiery","honest","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Skilled at tuning windmills to grind grain efficiently in shifting winds.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_quill","name":"Oren Quill","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy, stooped and ink-stained, with thick spectacles and a mind for shifting skybridge routes. He has charted the network for forty years.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To complete a definitive map of the skybridge network before his eyesight fails.","goal":"Publish a map that exposes which spans the Cartel has let decay while collecting tolls.","flaw":"He is a coward who avoids confrontation and hides behind scholarship.","internal_conflict":"He values neutral scholarship but knows his silence is helping the Cartel.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure the Academy to suppress maps that reveal neglected bridges.","arc":"Starts as a timid scholar who shelves his incriminating survey. After Isolde shows him a span that nearly killed a crew, he chooses to publish publicly despite Cartel threats. He ends as a voice of truth, having overcome his fear.","personality_traits":["gentle","absent-minded","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drifting skybridge networks with remarkable accuracy.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane blames Corvin Ashgrave's rising tolls for starving Warden repairs, and Corvin sees her as an obstacle to his monopoly, fuelling the 