{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her late thirties, with rope-scarred hands and a coat patched with cloudstone fibre. She grew up on Emberroost braiding cables beside her father, who fell when a spark severed a span. She is lean, sharp-eyed, and keeps a coil of cable at her belt.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To honour her father's death by making every skybridge spark-proof and safe to cross.","goal":"Force the archipelago to fund a full re-braiding of the central skybridges before the next season's storms.","flaw":"She trusts only her own calculations and refuses to delegate or accept help.","internal_conflict":"She fears that her obsession with safety is really guilt over not being present when her father died.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls in the Toll War starve the Wardens of repair funds and pit her against merchants.","arc":"Starts as a lone, controlling engineer who hoards every repair task. When a Cartel toll blockade leaves a skybridge failing, she must hand the cable-braiding to Hollow Circle volunteers and Cartel dockhands she distrusts. Seeing their work hold, she ends as a leader who shares authority and eases her guilt.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","protective","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and repairing cloudstone cables under tension.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Span Sense","description":"Can judge a skybridge's strain by feel and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","name":"Corvin Ashgrave","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties, with rings on every finger and a velvet coat dyed the colour of dusk. He rose from a dockhand's child at Mistral Docks to command a fleet of wind-skiffs.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure permanent control of inter-isle trade so his family never knows poverty again.","goal":"Make the Cartel's tolls and grain levy permanent law across the archipelago.","flaw":"He treats every person as a transaction and cannot believe in loyalty that is not paid for.","internal_conflict":"He despises the desperation of his own childhood yet is becoming the exploiter who created it.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle resists his grain levy and the Wardens expose his toll profiteering.","arc":"Starts as a confident monopolist who sees tolls as fair business. When the Hollow Circle's grain refusal strands his fleet and Isolde's repairs shame his claims, he is forced to bargain from weakness. He ends by capping the tolls, uneasily facing the cost of his greed.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","proud","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates and persuades through flattery and leverage.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Mastery","description":"Knows every wind-current and shipping lane between the isles.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reed","name":"Tamsin Reed","description":"A young, freckled miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted braids and sun-browned arms. She inherited her family windmill during the Grain Levy dispute and speaks plainly.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep her family's mill independent and her neighbours fed.","goal":"Organise the Hollow Circle to refuse the Cartel levy without starting a famine.","flaw":"She is impulsive and acts on anger before weighing consequences.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her community but fears she is too young and inexperienced to lead it.","external_conflict":"Corvin's Cartel levy on grain shipments threatens to bankrupt the Hollow's mills.","arc":"Starts as a hot-headed miller who wants to burn the Cartel's grain contracts. After Isolde warns that open flame could sever a skybridge, she chooses a disciplined grain boycott instead. She ends as a measured leader the Hollow Circle trusts.","personality_traits":["fiery","honest","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Skilled at tuning windmills to grind grain efficiently in shifting winds.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_quill","name":"Oren Quill","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy, stooped and ink-stained, with thick spectacles and a mind for shifting skybridge routes. He has charted the network for forty years.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To complete a definitive map of the skybridge network before his eyesight fails.","goal":"Publish a map that exposes which spans the Cartel has let decay while collecting tolls.","flaw":"He is a coward who avoids confrontation and hides behind scholarship.","internal_conflict":"He values neutral scholarship but knows his silence is helping the Cartel.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure the Academy to suppress maps that reveal neglected bridges.","arc":"Starts as a timid scholar who shelves his incriminating survey. After Isolde shows him a span that nearly killed a crew, he chooses to publish publicly despite Cartel threats. He ends as a voice of truth, having overcome his fear.","personality_traits":["gentle","absent-minded","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drifting skybridge networks with remarkable accuracy.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane blames Corvin Ashgrave's rising tolls for starving Warden repairs, and Corvin sees her as an obstacle to his monopoly, fuelling the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_corvin_tamsin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Ashgrave imposes the grain levy on Tamsin Reed's mill, and she defies him, escalating the Grain Levy conflict."},{"id":"rel_isolde_tamsin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vane steers Tamsin Reed away from open flame toward a disciplined boycott, forming an uneasy alliance against the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_oren_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_oren_quill","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Oren Quill taught Isolde Vane to read skybridge maps, and his hidden survey of neglected spans could either aid or endanger her campaign."}]}
