{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","description":"A sharp-tongued Bridge Warden inspector in her late thirties, raised in the cable-braiding sheds of Emberroost. Wind-burned and wiry, she wears a soot-stained warden coat and carries a coil of cloudstone thread at her belt. Years of auditing skybridge failures have left her convinced that every accident has a paying culprit.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that recent skybridge failures are deliberate sabotage rather than bad luck, honouring the Warden who trained her and died in one.","goal":"Expose who is severing skybridges and produce evidence that will stand before the Wardens' council.","flaw":"Sarcasm used as armour; she mocks allies until they stop offering help.","internal_conflict":"She distrusts everyone yet cannot finish the investigation without relying on others.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls and the Toll War make her inquiries politically toxic and endanger her life.","arc":"Starts as a lone, cynical inspector who treats colleagues as liabilities. When a severed skybridge near Emberroost strands a crew she had dismissed, she must accept Ilsa's help and publicly credit it to reach the evidence. She ends as a leader who trusts a team and uses her wit to rally people rather than push them away.","personality_traits":["sardonic","observant","stubborn","loyal in secret"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"Can tell from the fray pattern of a cloudstone cable whether it snapped from wear, a spark, or a blade.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Sharp Interrogation","description":"Uses dry wit to unsettle witnesses into revealing more than they intend.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_hale","name":"Corvin Hale","description":"A silver-haired Drift Cartel merchant prince with ring-laden fingers and a velvet voice, based at the Mistral Docks. He built his fortune on shipping contracts and has quietly profited from every closure of a skybridge.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To make the Cartel the sole owner of every shipping lane so no rival can undercut him again, as happened when his father was ruined.","goal":"Force the Wardens to cede bridge-toll authority to the Cartel by making the bridges appear unsafe.","flaw":"Hubris; he believes any person or law can be bought.","internal_conflict":"He claims to act for the Cartel's prosperity but fears he is only repeating his father's greedy mistakes.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle's resistance to the Grain Levy and Mara's investigation threaten to expose his scheme.","arc":"Begins as a confident, untouchable financier who orders quiet sabotage. When the Hollow Circle refuses the Grain Levy and the wind-debt ledgers start to unravel, he escalates and cuts a critical bridge, stranding his own cargo fleet. He ends ruined and forced to testify, finally confronting that his greed mirrors his father's.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market Manipulation","description":"Steers tolls, wind-debt rates and cargo prices to squeeze rivals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_thorne","name":"Ilsa Thorne","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers and a habit of muttering coordinates. She charts the shifting skybridge network and has noticed anomalies in the maps that match no natural drift.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove her maps are right after the Academy dismissed her anomaly reports as errors.","goal":"Trace the pattern of anomalies to the exact bridges being targeted.","flaw":"Naive; she shares findings with anyone who flatters her work.","internal_conflict":"She craves academic validation yet suspects the truth will cost her place at the Academy.","external_conflict":"Academy elders, quietly indebted to the Cartel, suppress her charts.","arc":"Starts as a timid junior whose reports are ignored and who trusts the wrong flatterers. After a Cartel agent steals a chart she shared freely, she chooses to hand her unpublished maps directly to Mara. She ends as a confident witness who stands before the council to present her evidence.","personality_traits":["curious","anxious","precise","earnest"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Predicts island and bridge positions weeks ahead from wind data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_oakley","name":"Bram Oakley","description":"A broad, quiet miller of the Hollow Circle with flour-dusted forearms, who leads the resistance to the Grain Levy from his windmill on The Hollow.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his neighbours from starving after the Cartel's levy, remembering the hardship of the Great Calm told by his grandmother.","goal":"Overturn the Grain Levy without open violence.","flaw":"Stubborn pride; he refuses help from anyone he considers an outsider.","internal_conflict":"He values peace but is tempted to burn Cartel cargo in anger.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers press the Hollow Circle to pay the levy or lose their wind-debt standing.","arc":"Begins as a stubborn holdout who refuses outside aid. When Cartel enforcers seize a grain barge and wind-debt threatens his village, he swallows his pride and allies with Mara to share grain-shipping records. He ends as a negotiator who wins the levy's repeal without resorting to fire.","personality_traits":["patient","gruff","principled","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Logistics","description":"Knows exactly how much grain every isle needs and when.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Voss suspects Corvin Hale is behind the skybridge sabotage, and he sees her inspections as a threat to his toll scheme."},{"id":"rel_corvin_mara_threat","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Hale tries to bribe, then discredit, Mara Voss to stop her investigation."},{"id":"rel_ilsa_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilsa_thorne","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilsa Thorne supplies Mara Voss with maps that reveal the sabotage pattern, while Mara's scorn tests their trust."},{"id":"rel_bram_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_bram_oakley","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Bram Oakley resists Corvin Hale's Grain Levy, which Corvin enforces to tighten Cartel control over the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_mara_bram_ally","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_bram_oakley","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Voss and Bram Oakley reluctantly share evidence, linking the grain shipment seizures to the bridge sabotage."}]}
