ng","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her neighbours from starvation and debt caused by the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Organise the Hollow Circle to withhold grain until the Grain Levy is repealed.","flaw":"Avoids confrontation and delays decisions until others force her hand.","internal_conflict":"She wants to keep the peace of the Hollow yet knows that peace is what lets the Cartel exploit them.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy drains her stores while Cartel agents pressure the Hollow Circle to comply.","arc":"Starts as a timid miller who hides behind ledgers and hopes the levy will pass. When a Cartel inspector seizes a neighbour's harvest and the family faces wind-debt ruin, she stands before the Circle and calls the grain strike. She ends as the Circle's resolute voice, no longer waiting to be pushed.","personality_traits":["quiet","observant","patient","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Memory","description":"Recalls every shipment, debt, and promise in the Hollow's records.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_quill","name":"Tobias Quill","description":"A 52-year-old cartographer at Silverspine Academy, thin and ink-stained with spectacles on a chain and a habit of muttering coordinates. He has charted the skybridge network for thirty years and has noticed anomalies in the ice-cold currents beneath the isles that no one will believe.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove the shifting currents and failing spans are signs of something vast below, vindicating his life's work.","goal":"Convince the Wardens and a royal house to fund an expedition into the frozen depths.","flaw":"Obsessive and tactless, he alienates the very people he needs to convince.","internal_conflict":"He craves academic recognition but fears his findings are a delusion built from loneliness.","external_conflict":"Academy elders di