ridge load figures, and a limp from a cable snap he never discusses.","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe for everyone regardless of how much debt they owe.","goal":"Prove the Cartel's tolls are diverting funds meant for bridge maintenance.","flaw":"He clings to rules and procedure even when they protect the wrong people.","internal_conflict":"His oath to the Wardens demands he arrest Kessa, but her stolen records could prove what he has long suspected.","external_conflict":"Warden leadership wants quiet compromise in the Toll War, while the Cartel pressures him to turn over fugitives.","arc":"Toma starts as a by-the-book surveyor who follows every order. When Kessa shows him the Cartel's falsified maintenance accounts, he chooses to hide her instead of arresting her. He ends as a Warden willing to break procedure to protect the bridges.","personality_traits":["methodical","honest","stubborn","kind"],"abilities":[{"name":"Structural Insight","description":"Spots weak points in skybridges and cable work by sight and touch.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Warden Standing","description":"His rank gets him access to Academy archives and bridge records.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_maren_holt","name":"Maren Holt","role":"supporting","description":"A weathered, sharp-tongued miller and elder of the Hollow Circle, with flour-dusted forearms and a stern gaze. She has organized the Hollow's resistance to the Grain Levy and keeps its ledgers in her head.","motivation":"To keep the Hollow's grain feeding the isles without Cartel strangulation.","goal":"Secure proof of the Cartel's levy fraud to turn other isles against the Grain Levy.","flaw":"She distrusts outsiders so deeply that she rejects allies who could help her.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her people from violence yet knows resistance may require it.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to starve the Hollow's mills, and Cartel enforcers are leaning on her neighbors to break ranks.","arc":"Maren begins as an isolated elder who refuses all outside help. When Kessa brings her a copy of the Cartel's levy records and Orsolo's enforcers burn a grain barge, she chooses to join a wider coalition of isles. She ends as the leader of an alliance rather than a lone holdout.","personality_traits":["stern","loyal","pragmatic","tough"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community Command","description":"Rallies the farmers and millers of the Hollow to act as one.","category":"social"},{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Tracks supply and shipments with uncanny accuracy to spot fraud.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kessa_orsolo_hunted","source_character_id":"chr_orsolo_brask","target_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolo Brask has put a price on Kessa Vane's head for stealing the Cartel's ledger-mind, and he hunts her relentlessly across the archipelago."},{"id":"rel_kessa_toma_uneasy_ally","source_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","target_character_id":"chr_toma_reyl","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kessa Vane and Toma Reyl form an uneasy alliance when she gives him proof of Cartel fraud, though his oath to arrest her keeps the bond strained."},{"id":"rel_maren_orsolo_levy","source_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","target_character_id":"chr_orsolo_brask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Holt openly defies Orsolo Brask's Grain Levy, and he responds by leaning on the Hollow's neighbors to isolate her."},{"id":"rel_kessa_maren_records","source_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","target_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kessa Vane supplies Maren Holt with Cartel levy records, but Maren's distrust of outsiders makes her accept the gift reluctantly."}]}
