{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kessa_vane","name":"Kessa Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed rigger in her early thirties, Kessa grew up on the cable catwalks of Emberroost and learned to read skybridge ledgers the way others read faces. She sells her skill at slipping through guild records and wind-debt registries to anyone who pays. She wears a soot-stained flight coat, a cracked brass monocle, and a perpetual smirk she uses to hide how tired she is.","motivation":"To erase the crushing wind-debt her family has carried for three generations and finally stop owing anyone.","goal":"Steal the Drift Cartel's sealed ledger-mind from Mistral Docks and sell it for enough to buy her family's freedom.","flaw":"She trusts no one and treats every ally as a future betrayer, so she sabotages help before it can be given.","internal_conflict":"She despises the Cartel's grip on debt yet is coming to see herself as just another seller of people's secrets.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel has marked her as the most wanted thief in the archipelago, and Bridge Wardens are closing in on her stolen cargo routes.","arc":"Kessa begins as a lone cynic who sees every person as a transaction. When Toma Reyl risks his post to hide her from Cartel hunters at Silverspine, she must choose between selling the ledger-mind for her own freedom or releasing the debt records to everyone. She releases them, ending as someone who accepts help and puts the debt of many above her own.","personality_traits":["cynical","quick-witted","guarded","resourceful","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Slicing","description":"Forges and alters wind-debt registries and crossing seals without leaving traces.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Cable Running","description":"Moves swiftly along skybridge cables and catwalks without tools or safety lines.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cold Read","description":"Sizes up a mark's weaknesses within moments of meeting them.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":null},{"id":"chr_orsolo_brask","name":"Orsolo Brask","role":"antagonist","description":"A heavyset, silver-bearded merchant prince of the Drift Cartel who rules the Mistral Docks shipping lanes from a glass-walled counting house. He wears rings stamped with the sigils of debtor houses and speaks softly, never raising his voice because he never needs to.","motivation":"To make the Cartel's hold on every crossing permanent, and to be remembered as the one who finished the Charter's work.","goal":"Recover the stolen ledger-mind and make an example of Kessa so no one dares to touch Cartel records again.","flaw":"His arrogance blinds him to threats from those he considers beneath him.","internal_conflict":"He claims to protect trade for everyone, yet he knows his tolls are starving the very isles he says he serves.","external_conflict":"The Toll War with the Bridge Wardens and the Hollow Circle's resistance to the Grain Levy threaten to expose his debt-ledger.","arc":"Orsolo starts as a confident ruler certain the Cartel cannot be touched. After the ledger-mind's contents spread and the Hollow Circle refuses the Grain Levy, he overreaches by burning a Warden bridge crossing in the open. He ends stripped of authority and forced to face the debts he created.","personality_traits":["patient","calculating","courteous","ruthless","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Binds rivals and officials through carefully held wind-debts and favors.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade Network","description":"Commands informants and hired hunters in every harbor of the archipelago.","category":"other"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_toma_reyl","name":"Toma Reyl","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered, soft-spoken Bridge Warden surveyor stationed at Silverspine Academy. He has weathered hands, a notebook full of bridge load figures, and a limp from a cable snap he never discusses.","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe for everyone regardless of how much debt they owe.","goal":"Prove the Cartel's tolls are diverting funds meant for bridge maintenance.","flaw":"He clings to rules and procedure even when they protect the wrong people.","internal_conflict":"His oath to the Wardens demands he arrest Kessa, but her stolen records could prove what he has long suspected.","external_conflict":"Warden leadership wants quiet compromise in the Toll War, while the Cartel pressures him to turn over fugitives.","arc":"Toma starts as a by-the-book surveyor who follows every order. When Kessa shows him the Cartel's falsified maintenance accounts, he chooses to hide her instead of arresting her. He ends as a Warden willing to break procedure to protect the bridges.","personality_traits":["methodical","honest","stubborn","kind"],"abilities":[{"name":"Structural Insight","description":"Spots weak points in skybridges and cable work by sight and touch.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Warden Standing","description":"His rank gets him access to Academy archives and bridge records.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_maren_holt","name":"Maren Holt","role":"supporting","description":"A weathered, sharp-tongued miller and elder of the Hollow Circle, with flour-dusted forearms and a stern gaze. She has organized the Hollow's resistance to the Grain Levy and keeps its ledgers in her head.","motivation":"To keep the Hollow's grain feeding the isles without Cartel strangulation.","goal":"Secure proof of the Cartel's levy fraud to turn other isles against the Grain Levy.","flaw":"She distrusts outsiders so deeply that she rejects allies who could help her.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her people from violence yet knows resistance may require it.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to starve the Hollow's mills, and Cartel enforcers are leaning on her neighbors to break ranks.","arc":"Maren begins as an isolated elder who refuses all outside help. When Kessa brings her a copy of the Cartel's levy records and Orsolo's enforcers burn a grain barge, she chooses to join a wider coalition of isles. She ends as the leader of an alliance rather than a lone holdout.","personality_traits":["stern","loyal","pragmatic","tough"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community Command","description":"Rallies the farmers and millers of the Hollow to act as one.","category":"social"},{"name":"Grain Reckoning","description":"Tracks supply and shipments with uncanny accuracy to spot fraud.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kessa_orsolo_hunted","source_character_id":"chr_orsolo_brask","target_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolo Brask has put a price on Kessa Vane's head for stealing the Cartel's ledger-mind, and he hunts her relentlessly across the archipelago."},{"id":"rel_kessa_toma_uneasy_ally","source_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","target_character_id":"chr_toma_reyl","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kessa Vane and Toma Reyl form an uneasy alliance when she gives him proof of Cartel fraud, though his oath to arrest her keeps the bond strained."},{"id":"rel_maren_orsolo_levy","source_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","target_character_id":"chr_orsolo_brask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Holt openly defies Orsolo Brask's Grain Levy, and he responds by leaning on the Hollow's neighbors to isolate her."},{"id":"rel_kessa_maren_records","source_character_id":"chr_kessa_vane","target_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kessa Vane supplies Maren Holt with Cartel levy records, but Maren's distrust of outsiders makes her accept the gift reluctantly."}]}
