asive man hiding a past failure. When Marguerite confronts him with proof he was inspecting the manor's cables during the murder, he confesses the old failure publicly. He ends clear of suspicion and honest with the Wardens.","personality_traits":["quiet","anxious","skilled","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Braids and inspects cloudstone cable with expert precision.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_silas_fennick","name":"Silas Fennick","description":"A genial, round-faced miller from The Hollow, in his forties, with flour-dusted sleeves and a booming laugh. He attends as the Hollow Circle's representative on the grain levy.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"He wants to end the Cartel levy that is starving his neighbours.","goal":"Keep his role in the victim's death hidden while still forcing the levy to be abandoned.","flaw":"He justifies harmful acts as necessary for the common good.","internal_conflict":"His kindness conflicts with the violence he committed in a moment of rage.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy puts him in direct opposition to Ottoline, and Marguerite's inquiry closes in on him.","arc":"He starts as a warm, trusted guest who has killed in anger. When Marguerite shows that windmill grain dust was on the victim's study door, he tries to blame Tobias, then breaks down under the weight of that choice. He ends by confessing, accepting responsibility for the act he had justified.","personality_traits":["jovial","protective","secretive","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Easy Rapport","description":"Quickly earns trust and deflects suspicion with humour.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_alder","name":"Wren Alder","description":"A young manor servant of nineteen, freckled and quick, who grew up on Mistral Docks and carries trays and messages through the house. She sees and hears far more than guests assume.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"She wants to repay her family's wind-debt so they can leave Cartel service.","goal":"Earn enough from the weekend to clear the debt without losing her post.","flaw":"She stays silent when speaking up might cost her position.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between loyalty to her employer and the truth she witnessed.","external_conflict":"Ottoline threatens her family's debt if she repeats what she overheard.","arc":"She begins as a silent servant who saw Silas near the study. When Marguerite gently asks her directly, she chooses to testify despite Ottoline's threat. She ends as a witness whose courage frees her from the fear that kept her quiet.","personality_traits":["quick","watchful","nervous","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Unseen Presence","description":"Moves through rooms unnoticed and overhears private talk.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marguerite_tobias","source_character_id":"chr_marguerite_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_hale","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marguerite Vane is Tobias Hale's estranged aunt and cautious ally, whose suspicion of him strains the tie until she tests his alibi."},{"id":"rel_ottoline_marguerite","source_character_id":"chr_ottoline_brask","target_character_id":"chr_marguerite_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ottoline Brask tries to block Marguerite Vane's inquiry because it threatens to expose the Cartel's toll ledgers."},{"id":"rel_silas_ottoline","source_character_id":"chr_silas_fennick","target_character_id":"chr_ottoline_brask","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Silas Fennick resents Ottoline Brask for the grain levy, and that resentment drove the confrontation that ended in the murder."},{"id":"rel_ottoline_wren","source_character_id":"chr_ottoline_brask","target_character_id":"chr_wren_alder","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Ottoline Brask holds Wren Alder's family debt over her to keep her silent about what she saw."},{"id":"rel_silas_tobias","source_character_id":"chr_silas_fennick","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Silas Fennick deflects blame onto Tobias Hale, exploiting Tobias's evasiveness to protect himself."}]}
