r-cased receiver and is rarely seen in the light. Her real interest is the cabin's transmitter, which she believes can be used to see Cartel profits before they happen.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To seize the future-seeing transmitter so the Cartel can profit from knowing outcomes before rivals do, securing her promotion.","goal":"Take control of the cabin's radio and silence Mara before she broadcasts anything that exposes the Cartel.","flaw":"Treats people as instruments and cannot imagine anyone refusing a fair price.","internal_conflict":"She fears the transmissions will reveal her own failure, yet cannot stop listening for it.","external_conflict":"The Toll War has made the Cartel suspicious of its own agents, so a failed acquisition would end her career, while Mara refuses every offer.","arc":"Sera begins as a confident agent who believes everything has a price. When she hears a future broadcast of her own ruin through Mara's radio after Mara refuses her offer, she tries to destroy the transmitter and is left stranded in the dark with the static. She ends the story broken, finally confronting the limits of leverage.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","patient","cold"],"abilities":[{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Reads desperation and builds offers that are hard to refuse.","category":"social"},{"name":"Silver Receiver","description":"A Cartel device that can eavesdrop on distant broadcasts.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobin_bond","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Mara Veln relies on Tobin Harrow's weekly deliveries and company, but her future-voice broadcast naming him as the next to vanish strains their friendship with fear and secrecy."},{"id":"rel_sera_mara_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sera Quill pressures Mara Veln to sell or surrender the cabin's transmitter, escalating from bribery to threats when Mara refuses."},{"id":"rel_sera_tobin_leverage","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_harrow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sera Quill uses the Grain Levy audit to threaten Tobin Harrow's mill, trying to force him to isolate Mara from the Hollow Circle."}]}
