[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered former sky-pirate in her late thirties, Kestrel once raided cartel cargo skiffs from the wind-lanes above Mistral Docks before surrendering her ship and taking a pardon. She wears a patched crimson coat, has a rope-scarred left palm, and keeps a cold pipe she never lights, honoring the ban on open flame aloft.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To prove her pardon was earned by recovering the stolen map that her old crew is blamed for taking.","goal":"Recover the stolen skybridge map before the season's wind-debt falls due and clear her name.","flaw":"Reckless pride that makes her rush into duels and bargains alone.","internal_conflict":"She misses the thrill of piracy and fears she is only a pirate in disguise.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel suspects her of the theft and holds her pardon hostage while she races rivals across the isles.","arc":"Starts as a proud lone operator who trusts only her blade. At Silverspine, she must choose between stealing the map back by force or accepting the Wardens' help, and she chooses to share credit and risk. She ends as a trusted ally who proves her reform through partnership rather than bravado.","personality_traits":["bold","wry","guarded","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloud-Rigging","description":"Expert at sailing skiffs and swinging across skybridge cables in high wind.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Smuggler's Tongue","description":"Reads dockside crowds and talks past cartel inspectors.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_thane","name":"Orsolya Thane","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-haired Drift Cartel merchant princess in her fifties, polished and patient. She operates from a glass-walled counting house at Mistral Docks and wears rings stamped with the Cartel Charter seal.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the map so the Cartel alone controls every future skybridge route.","goal":"Seize the map and use it to raise tolls and tighten the Cartel's hold on trade.","flaw":"Arrogant belief that everything, including loyalty, has a price.","internal_conflict":"She is haunted by the fear that her power rests on debts rather than respect.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and Grain Levy turn the Wardens and Hollow Circle against her while Kestrel races to the map first.","arc":"Starts as a confident broker who sees people as ledgers. When the Hollow Circle refuses her levy and its millers withhold grain, her bribes fail and her own captains waver. She ends exposed and stripped of leverage, forced to bargain as an equal.","personality_traits":["calculating","charming","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Binds people through accrued wind-debt and favors.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_ashgrove","name":"Bram Ashgrove","role":"supporting","description":"A broad, soot-stained Bridge Warden engineer in his forties, stationed at Emberroost, where he braids cloudstone cable. He carries a shielded lantern and a worn splicing kit.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe from tolls that starve their upkeep.","goal":"Use the map to find failing bridge sections and repair them before one collapses.","flaw":"Rigid rule-following that makes him distrust anyone with a criminal past.","internal_conflict":"He values safety above all but suspects the Wardens' rules protect the powerful.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls cut Warden funding while Kestrel's pirate record clashes with his duty to uphold order.","arc":"Starts as a distrustful stickler who refuses to work with Kestrel. When a cable frays during a storm crossing and she saves a crew by breaking a Warden rule, he chooses to vouch for her. He ends as a flexible ally who bends rules for people's safety.","personality_traits":["stubborn","dutiful","practical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Repairs and reinforces skybridge cable under strain.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_marrow","name":"Ilse Marrow","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers and cropped copper hair. She charted the stolen map's original survey and remembers most of it.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To protect the academy's honest record of the shifting skybridges from being monopolized.","goal":"Reconstruct the map from memory and publish it openly before the Cartel can hoard it.","flaw":"Timidity that makes her stay silent when she should speak.","internal_conflict":"She wants scholarly neutrality but feels guilty that her own survey enabled the theft.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents watch Silverspine and pressure the academy to hand over her notes.","arc":"Starts as a nervous scholar hiding her notes. When Cartel agents threaten the academy and Kestrel shields her, Ilse chooses to share her reconstruction publicly. She ends as a confident voice who speaks when it matters.","personality_traits":["observant","anxious","brilliant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Eidetic Charting","description":"Recalls routes and survey details with near-perfect accuracy.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","description":"A genial miller and Hollow Circle elder in his sixties, with floury forearms and a sun-creased face, who runs the largest windmill on The Hollow.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep The Hollow's grain free of the Cartel levy.","goal":"Win allies against the Grain Levy and keep feeding the archipelago.","flaw":"Stubborn conservatism that makes him resist any change to old ways.","internal_conflict":"He prizes peace but knows resisting the Cartel may require confrontation.","external_conflict":"The Cartel levy threatens his mill's survival and tempts neighbors to submit.","arc":"Starts as a peaceful holdout who refuses to take sides. After Orsolya's agents seize a grain shipment, he chooses to hide Kestrel and trade grain for her help. He ends as an active ally who accepts the risk of open resistance.","personality_traits":["warm","patient","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Predicts gusts and storms from windmill behavior.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kestrel_orsolya","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Thane holds Kestrel Vane's pardon over her and suspects her of the theft, using it to pressure Kestrel into delivering the map to the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_kestrel_bram","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_bram_ashgrove","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Kestrel Vane and Bram Ashgrove clash over her pirate past and his rigid rules, though they later become reluctant allies."},{"id":"rel_ilse_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilse Marrow provides Kestrel Vane with map knowledge while Kestrel protects her from Cartel agents."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_tobias","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Thane imposes the Grain Levy on Tobias Wren, who resists and drives conflict between the Cartel and the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_tobias_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobias Wren shelters Kestrel Vane and trades grain for her aid against the Cartel."}]}
