{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_marta_voss","name":"Marta Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered caravan-mistress in her late forties who leads the Windlark, a string of cargo skiffs that haul goods across Aetheria's skybridges. She has a sunburnt face, silver-streaked braids tied with copper wire, and a patched coat that smells of lamp oil. Born in the grain isle of The Hollow, she bought her first skiff with a decade of milling wages and has kept her crew fed and paid through lean seasons ever since.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep her found-family crew safe, fed, and out of debt so none of them ever have to return to hungry isles.","goal":"Deliver a full caravan of grain to Mistral Docks and clear every crew member's wind-debt before the season ends.","flaw":"Stubborn pride that makes her refuse help and shoulder every burden alone.","internal_conflict":"She longs to retire and rest but fears that without her command the crew will scatter.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and the Grain Levy make every crossing costlier, and the Drift Cartel squeezes her cargo margins.","arc":"Marta starts as a lone, proud leader who hoards every decision and risk. When the Cartel levy and blocked bridges threaten to bankrupt the caravan, she must either abandon her pride or lose the crew, and she chooses to ask the Bridge Wardens for aid and share command with Tobin and Ilsa. She ends as a leader who trusts her crew to carry the caravan on without her.","personality_traits":["warm","stubborn","resourceful","protective","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Reads drift currents and cloud banks to find the safest crossing windows.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hard Bargaining","description":"Negotiates fair prices and wind-debt terms with dockside merchants.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_hale","name":"Tobin Hale","role":"supporting","description":"A lanky nineteen-year-old skiff-hand with ink-stained fingers and a satchel of sketched maps. Orphaned in the Great Calm's aftermath stories he grew up on, he was taken in by Marta at fifteen. He has wind-tousled brown hair and a crooked grin, and he idolises the cartographers of Silverspine.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To earn a place at Silverspine Academy and chart a skybridge route no one has mapped.","goal":"Produce an accurate map of the shifting bridges along the caravan route to win an Academy scholarship.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity that leads him to wander off the safe path.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between loyalty to Marta's caravan and his dream of leaving it behind.","external_conflict":"The Toll War closes bridges he needs to survey, and Cartel guards confiscate unregistered maps.","arc":"Tobin begins as an impulsive dreamer who treats the caravan as a stepping stone. When he scouts a closed bridge and nearly causes a collapse, his map saves the caravan from a Cartel ambush. He ends by choosing to apprentice with the Wardens while promising to chart routes for the crew, reconciling ambition with loyalty.","personality_traits":["curious","impulsive","eager","kind"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cartography","description":"Sketches precise maps of drifting bridge networks from memory.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Rigging Agility","description":"Climbs cables and skiff masts quickly and without fear.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","name":"Ilsa Brandt","role":"supporting","description":"The caravan's quartermaster, a broad-shouldered woman of fifty with iron-grey hair and a ledger always under her arm. A former Emberroost cable-braider, she left the forges after a spark accident severed a bridge and cost her partner his life. She is meticulous and quiet, and carries a small cloudstone charm.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To make sure no preventable accident ever kills anyone under her care again.","goal":"Keep the caravan's cargo and flame-safety protocols flawless through every crossing.","flaw":"Rigid perfectionism that makes her distrust any plan she did not write.","internal_conflict":"She feels guilty for the Emberroost accident and fears she is destined to fail again.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure her to bend the no-open-flame rule for faster shipping.","arc":"Ilsa starts as a guilt-driven enforcer who micro-manages every detail. When a Cartel saboteur lights a flame near a bridge, she must improvise a shield from cargo tarps rather than follow her protocol, and succeeds. She ends able to forgive herself and delegate safety duties to the crew.","personality_traits":["meticulous","quiet","loyal","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Repairs cloudstone cables and bridge fittings in the field.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Cargo Accounting","description":"Tracks goods and wind-debts without error.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dray","name":"Corvin Dray","role":"antagonist","description":"A sleek Drift Cartel factor in his forties with oiled black hair, rings on every finger, and a velvet coat in cartel gold. Raised in Mistral Docks' counting-houses, he rose by turning other people's debts into leverage. He speaks softly and smiles often, and he is certain that order comes from control of the shipping lanes.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a seat among the Cartel's merchant princes by proving he can bring every caravan under Cartel contract.","goal":"Force Marta's caravan to sign an exclusive hauling contract by calling in its wind-debts.","flaw":"Overconfident belief that everyone can be bought or bound by debt.","internal_conflict":"He privately envies the loyalty free crews show each other, which no contract has ever bought him.","external_conflict":"His superiors demand results, while the Wardens and Hollow Circle resist the tolls and levies he enforces.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident debt-broker who trusts only leverage. When Marta's crew refuses his contract and the Wardens expose his inflated tolls in front of the docks, his scheme collapses publicly. He ends stripped of his post and left to face a life without leverage, with a final chance to honour a debt he forgives.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","patient","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt records to pressure rivals into compliance.","category":"social"},{"name":"Network of Informants","description":"Tracks caravan movements through dock spies.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sera_quill","name":"Sera Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed Bridge Warden engineer in her thirties, with cropped red hair, soot-smudged cheeks and a tool belt hung with cloudstone gauges. Trained at Silverspine, she travels the bridges inspecting cables. She is honest to a fault and impatient with merchants.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and toll-free for those who cannot afford Cartel prices.","goal":"Document the Cartel's illegal toll hikes and bring proof before the Wardens' council.","flaw":"Self-righteous inflexibility that alienates potential allies.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her strict rules sometimes harm the very poor travellers she wants to protect.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pits her Wardens against Cartel enforcers who obstruct her inspections.","arc":"Sera starts as a rigid inspector who treats merchants as enemies. When Marta shelters her from Cartel pursuit, she sees caravans as allies and shares her evidence with the crew. She ends by negotiating a Warden-caravan safe-passage pact, softening her rule-bound stance.","personality_traits":["honest","blunt","diligent","brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Structural Inspection","description":"Detects stress fractures in cloudstone bridges by touch and sound.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marta_tobin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Marta Voss took in Tobin Hale as a teen and mentors him, but her wish to keep him close clashes with his dream of leaving for Silverspine."},{"id":"rel_marta_ilsa_ally","source_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marta Voss relies on quartermaster Ilsa Brandt as her closest confidante, though Ilsa's rigid protocols often collide with Marta's improvisation."},{"id":"rel_corvin_marta_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dray targets Marta Voss's caravan, using its wind-debts and the Grain Levy to coerce an exclusive Cartel contract."},{"id":"rel_corvin_ilsa_rival","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Dray pressures Ilsa Brandt to bend the no-flame rule for speed, and Ilsa refuses, making them bitter rivals over safety versus profit."},{"id":"rel_sera_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sera Quill is gathering proof of the illegal tolls Corvin Dray enforces, putting the Warden engineer directly against the Cartel factor."},{"id":"rel_sera_marta_ally","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sera Quill and Marta Voss grow from wary strangers into allies when Marta shelters the Warden and they combine evidence and safe passage."},{"id":"rel_tobin_sera_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"ch