uperiors demand results, while the Wardens and Hollow Circle resist the tolls and levies he enforces.","arc":"Corvin begins as a confident debt-broker who trusts only leverage. When Marta's crew refuses his contract and the Wardens expose his inflated tolls in front of the docks, his scheme collapses publicly. He ends stripped of his post and left to face a life without leverage, with a final chance to honour a debt he forgives.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","patient","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt records to pressure rivals into compliance.","category":"social"},{"name":"Network of Informants","description":"Tracks caravan movements through dock spies.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sera_quill","name":"Sera Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed Bridge Warden engineer in her thirties, with cropped red hair, soot-smudged cheeks and a tool belt hung with cloudstone gauges. Trained at Silverspine, she travels the bridges inspecting cables. She is honest to a fault and impatient with merchants.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and toll-free for those who cannot afford Cartel prices.","goal":"Document the Cartel's illegal toll hikes and bring proof before the Wardens' council.","flaw":"Self-righteous inflexibility that alienates potential allies.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her strict rules sometimes harm the very poor travellers she wants to protect.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pits her Wardens against Cartel enforcers who obstruct her inspections.","arc":"Sera starts as a rigid inspector who treats merchants as enemies. When Marta shelters her from Cartel pursuit, she sees caravans as allies and shares her evidence with the crew. She ends by negotiating a Warden-caravan safe-passage pact, softening her rule-bound stance.","personality_traits":["honest","blunt","diligent","brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Structural Inspection","description":"Detects stress fractures in cloudstone bridges by touch and sound.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marta_tobin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Marta Voss took in Tobin Hale as a teen and mentors him, but her wish to keep him close clashes with his dream of leaving for Silverspine."},{"id":"rel_marta_ilsa_ally","source_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Marta Voss relies on quartermaster Ilsa Brandt as her closest confidante, though Ilsa's rigid protocols often collide with Marta's improvisation."},{"id":"rel_corvin_marta_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dray targets Marta Voss's caravan, using its wind-debts and the Grain Levy to coerce an exclusive Cartel contract."},{"id":"rel_corvin_ilsa_rival","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","target_character_id":"chr_ilsa_brandt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Dray pressures Ilsa Brandt to bend the no-flame rule for speed, and Ilsa refuses, making them bitter rivals over safety versus profit."},{"id":"rel_sera_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_dray","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sera Quill is gathering proof of the illegal tolls Corvin Dray enforces, putting the Warden engineer directly against the Cartel factor."},{"id":"rel_sera_marta_ally","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"chr_marta_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sera Quill and Marta Voss grow from wary strangers into allies when Marta shelters the Warden and they combine evidence and safe passage."},{"id":"rel_tobin_sera_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_sera_quill","target_character_id":"ch